  "disclosure_status": "partially_disclosed",
  "notes": "The HF card's base_model field declares Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B (the released 128K-context base checkpoint), but the Qwen2.5-1M Technical Report states the 1M-context series was actually built from 'an intermediate checkpoint of pre-trained Qwen2.5' that still had only a 4K-token context length, i.e. an internal, unreleased pretraining checkpoint predating the public Qwen2.5-7B release, not the released Qwen2.5-7B artifact itself. From that intermediate checkpoint the model underwent 5 stages of progressive long-context pretraining (4K->32K->65,536->131,072->262,144 tokens; RoPE base raised 10,000->10,000,000), then a 2-stage long-context SFT (short sequences up to 32K, then mixed short/long up to 262K), then offline reinforcement learning on short (<=8K token) samples. The exact identity/weights of that intermediate checkpoint were not released, so it cannot be cited as a separate HF model_id.",
  "evidence": ["hf_readme_raw", "hf_api", "tech_report", "blog"]
 },
